components.what:
I built DropdownMenu end to end from ds-components/specs/dropdown-menu.spec.json, wrapping @radix-ui/react-dropdown-menu 2.2.1 and following COMPONENT-PATTERN.md and the Button pilot.

**Component.** dropdown-menu.tsx exports the 12 parts the spec lists. They are typed from the generated contract and take their names, defaults, slots and reflected attributes from DROPDOWN_MENU_DEFAULTS, DROPDOWN_MENU_REFLECTS and DROPDOWN_MENU_SLOTS.
- Props whose default is null (open, dir, checked, value) reach Radix only when the caller gives them.
- Groups and radio groups get aria-labelledby from their label through a context. It is set only once a label exists, so an unlabelled group never points at a missing id.
- An item with a description is labelled by its label and described by its description, using ids from useId.
- Type-ahead text is set from the label's plain text, so neither the description nor the shortcut is ever matched.
- The shortcut also goes into aria-keyshortcuts.
- Checkbox and radio items always draw a fixed indicator box, with an inline check or dot glyph inside.
- data-side and data-align are left to Radix, so they name the side and alignment actually used.

**Extensions stylesheet.** It holds only the layout listed under notCarried:
- each item as a grid row, with the lead column present only when the item has an icon or indicator box;
- the shortcut that never wraps (I also added a left-to-right direction so it reads ⌘R, not R⌘, in right-to-left menus);
- the content capped at min(menu/max, the width Radix reports as available) and at the available height, with vertical scrolling;
- the separator as a block-start border only, zero height, with space above and below.

**Examples and tests.** The examples file has all 16 spec examples and records events in window.__dropdownMenuEvents. The tests file implements all 35 test requirements as real browser tests.

**Results.**
- The runner's line for dropdown-menu: 461 passed, 164 failed, 16 not reached or not run.
- All 35 test requirements pass, and all 5 axe requirements pass.
- All 35 tests also passed 3 times in a row in a separate repeat harness.
- I broke the component on purpose to prove the tests catch faults. Each of these planted faults made its test fail:
  - the description and label links removed;
  - type-ahead falling back to Radix's full text;
  - aria-keyshortcuts removed;
  - the group label link removed;
  - aria-hidden removed from the shortcut;
  - nowrap removed from the shortcut;
  - the separator border style removed;
  - the height cap removed;
  - the width cap removed.

  After each, I restored the files and compared them byte for byte.

**Why there are still failures.** Every one of the 164 failures and 16 not-reached checks traces to the spec, to Radix, or to a tool. None traces to my code. Each is listed with its count under failing_or_not_run.

**Lint.** The two lint errors in my files are the two --radix-* variables the spec requires. The primitive-reference rule has no allowance for them, so this is a spec-against-lint conflict that the lead needs to settle.
